  "steps": [
    "Mix the buttermilk, hot sauce, and a pinch of salt and pepper in a bowl. Add the chicken and marinate at least 4 hours, or overnight.",
    "Mix the cabbage, mayo, vinegar, sugar, salt and pepper for the slaw and let it sit in the fridge while everything else cooks.",
    "Set up a breading station: leftover marinade in one bowl, and the flour, cornstarch, garlic powder, paprika, cayenne, salt and pepper in another.",
    "Dredge each piece in the flour mix, back into the buttermilk, then into the flour mix again. Press to coat well and rest on a rack for 10 minutes.",
    "Heat oil to 325 to 350F in a heavy skillet or Dutch oven. Fry until golden brown and 165F inside, about 5 to 7 minutes per side. Drain on a wire rack.",
    "Whisk 1/3 cup of the hot frying oil with the cayenne, brown sugar, garlic powder, paprika and chili powder until smooth.",
    "Brush the glaze generously over both sides of the chicken while it is still hot.",
    "Toast the buns in butter, then build with pickles, chicken and slaw."
  ]
